# XBD 4.6 Extended Security Controls
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XBD.4.6-extended-security-controls.001
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap04.html#4.6
class      untestable
says       Implementation-defined extended security controls do not change
           the semantics of any interface.
reason     What the controls are, and how to turn one on, is implementation-defined; a test cannot enable an unknown mechanism, and the interface tests of every other module already run with whatever controls the system has in force.
